## Phase 5 — The capabilities you didn't plan for

Ship after 1–4 are stable. Each is a config field, not a build.

- **`skills`** — SKILL.md loading from backend paths. Highest-value of the four; it is how consumers encode house style and playbooks without prompt-engineering every agent.
- **`memory`** — AGENTS.md files loaded into the system prompt at startup. Map to `memoryFiles` and validate paths exist at construction.
- **`interruptOn`** — per-tool HITL. Map to `approvals`. **Requires a checkpointer** — throw `AgentConfigError` at construction if approvals are set without one, rather than letting it fail at invoke.
- **`permissions`** — already used defensively in Phase 2; expose directly here.

